<title>USA: Johnson pact ups wages 22 pct over 3 years.</title>
<headline>Johnson pact ups wages 22 pct over 3 years.</headline>
<dateline>OBERLIN, Ohio 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Auto Workers said Friday that a tentative pact reached this week with Johnson Controls Inc calls for wages increasing 22 percent over three years.</p>
<p>The union, which reached a tentative pact with the Ford Motor seat-supplier Thursday, said the pact also calls for increased overtime pay and an immediate bonus of $1,000 for all members.</p>
<p>The 24-day strike by the United Auto Workers union at Johnson's seat-making plants in Oberlin, Ohio, and Plymouth, Michigan, had disrupted production of Ford's most profitable vehicles, the Expedition sport-utility vehicle.</p>
</text>
